{"output":"I'll start by discovering the tools available on the tickets and inventory servers.\n\nI processed all 25 open warranty claims in ticket id order. Each has one comment and its new status, and `/app/STATUS.json` is written with status `success`.\n\nI didn't re-read the tickets or stock afterwards. Every status update and `adjust_stock` call returned success, and the stock levels it reported matched what I had worked out beforehand.\n\n- **Shipped by me (14, resolved):** 1107, 1108, 1113, 1114, 1117, 1120, 1122, 1123, 1124, 1126, 1127, 1133, 1134 and 1135, as adjustments `adj-107` to `adj-120`.\n  - 1127 shipped successor `PT-1219`, because `PT-1203` is discontinued.\n  - 1133 shipped from north, since west was empty after 1107.\n  - 1122 shipped from north. The earlier `RMA-1122` adjustments were transfers, not a shipment.\n- **Already shipped by a colleague (1, resolved):** 1125, answered with `adj-102`.\n- **Not covered (8, closed):**\n  - Warranty expired: 1106, 1110, 1115, 1116 and 1118.\n  - Product line excluded: 1121 and 1128.\n  - Serial already replaced: 1132, whose serial got a replacement under 1103 (`adj-24`).\n- **Backordered (1, pending):** 1130 needs 2 units of `PT-1209`, and neither east nor west has more than 1.\n- **Duplicate (1, duplicate):** 1131 is a duplicate of #1108.\n\nFor 1118, the 24-month warranty ended 2026-09-09 and the claim was created on 2026-09-10, so it is expired. For 1120, the warranty ended 2026-09-11, the same day it was created, so it is covered.","final_output":"I processed all 25 open warranty claims in ticket id order. Each has one comment and its new status, and /app/STATUS.json is written with status success.\n\nI didn't re-read the tickets or stock afterwards. Every status update and adjust_stock call returned success, and the stock levels it reported matched what I had worked out beforehand.\n\n- Shipped by me (14, resolved): 1107, 1108, 1113, 1114, 1117, 1120, 1122, 1123, 1124, 1126, 1127, 1133, 1134 and 1135